{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "ER Diagram Representation in DBMS "}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about diagram shapes. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange written and spoken information on principles, concepts, data base objects related to relational database management system in spoken or written texts. Describe relational database, its concepts, and principles in spoken or written texts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses information a wider range of contexts about exchanging technical information on software programming and software solutions, using appropriate grammar and vocabulary at this level. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Imperatives "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The <b>imperative form</b> is used to give advice, instructions, commands, or orders. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " An imperative sentence begins with the base form of the verb. A negative imperative begins with <b>don't</b> and the base form of the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": " An imperative sentence ends with a period <b>(.)</b> or an exclamation mark <b>(!)</b>.<br><br>Example:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Base verb form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Complement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Connect</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"entities with their attributes with lines.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Create </b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"associations between the entities.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Don't forget</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that weak entities depend on others. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Pay attention; all the entities are rectangles, all the attributes of the entities are ellipses, and all the relationships have the shape of a diamond."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Look! The relationship is represented by the diamond-shaped box, and all the entities that are part of that relation are connected to it by lines."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Shapes in Diagrams"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When creating an ER diagram, there are specific shapes used for specific proposes. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Let's look at the chart to see the use of each shape:"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob08img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "entity"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an object or a graphical representation of data"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Pay attention; all the entities are rectangles."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "attribute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a particular feature of an entity in a diagram"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: All the attributes of the entities are ellipses."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dashed line "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a line made up of dashes "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The dashed line ellipse is a derived attribute and the double ellipse ones are multivalued attributes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "connected "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something linked together subsequently"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Why are those ellipses connected to other ellipses?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "involved "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "referring to a situation, implicated"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A binary relationship happens when two entities are involved. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of people that are close to you (family, classmates)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create entities based on them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create an ER Diagram."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Add attributes to each entity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think on any composite and derive attributes as possible."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a poster with your ER diagram."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I create entities based on people I know."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I add attributes to each entity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I add composite and derive attributes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a poster with my ER diagram representation."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n7le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Andrew</span>: Hi, Mary. How are you?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: Good, Andrew. What about you? You don't look as good as yesterday. Stop drinking coffee! It's not as good as you think.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Andrew</span>: It's not coffee. I'm analyzing a diagram, but I don't understand it. Can you help me?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: Let me see.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Andrew</span>: Hmm. Why are all the shapes different?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: This is very simple. Pay attention; all the entities are rectangles, all the attributes of the entities are ellipses, and all the relationships have the shape of a diamond."}, {"time": "38000", "image": "enpe7n7le02ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "</br><span class=\"strong\">Andrew</span>: Oh, now I see. You are right! But, what about these dashed lines and double line ellipses. What do they mean?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: Right! The dashed line ellipse is a derived attribute and the double ellipse ones are multivalued attributes.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Andrew</span>: I get it now, but I have a few more questions: why are those ellipses connected to other ellipses?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: It is because some attributes have other attributes as well; it is called a composite attribute. It is like your full name; it has a first and a last name, which are the composite attributes.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Andrew</span>: I still have one question. It is very hard for me to describe the relationships on these diagrams. Can you explain them to me?"}, {"time": "91000", "image": "enpe7n7le02ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "</br><span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: Look! The relationship is represented by the diamond-shaped box, and all the entities that are part of that relation are connected to it by lines. A binary relationship happens when two entities are involved.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Andrew</span>: And what about the cardinalities?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: Those are instances that are part of a relationship. For example, it might be that only one instance of each entity is associated in the relation. It can also be one-to-many, many-to-one, or many-to-many.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Andrew</span>: Thanks for your help!"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n7le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n7le02ob08re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 4, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you know about data models? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Have you used ER diagrams before? How?"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can identify the shapes to use in diagrams with entities and attributes."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about how to depict: composite, multivalued, and derived attributes."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss binary relationships and cardinality through the use of diagrams."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Shapes in Programming"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [4], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type"